# Checkov project basics

- Say **check** or **policy**, not "control". Shipped IDs are `CKV_<PROVIDER>_<N>` (Python) or `CKV2_<PROVIDER>_<N>` (YAML graph).
- Follow root `CONTRIBUTING.md` for issues, tests, pipenv/pre-commit, and PRs. Agent summary: `.cursor/skills/contributing.md`.
- New engineers: run `onboard-engineer` first (env, smoke test, first-hour path). See `AGENTS.md`.
- Python Terraform checks live in `checkov/terraform/checks/resource/<provider>/` (also `data/` / `provider/`). YAML graph checks live in `checkov/terraform/checks/graph_checks/<provider>/`.
- GRC requests use the **GRC new check request** GitHub issue form. Engineers implement them with the `add-terraform-check` skill (`gh issue view`, comment mapping questions on the issue, then scaffold check + tests). Record IaC assumptions on the PR. Label new-check issues/PRs `fast-lane`.
- Contribution skills follow SDLC in `AGENTS.md`: plan → design → develop → review → test → deploy. Do not finish a later phase from an earlier skill. New skills/rules need a `## SDLC` block (see `.cursor/rules/skill-sdlc.mdc`).
- Before human review: `review-check-quality`. Before/while opening a PR: `prepare-ci-ready-pr`. PM briefs: `scope-contribution`. QA fixtures: `qa-fixture-review`. Cloud Build / GitHub Actions / Jenkins / consumer image pins: `maintain-ci-runners`.
- New checks need pass **and** fail fixtures parsed through the **runner**. Assert **which resource IDs** pass/fail, not only counts. Do not hand-build conf dicts (see CONTRIBUTING / `test_IAMAdminPolicyDocument.py`).
- Prefer `pipenv run pytest` and `pre-commit`; disclose `.venv`/`uv` fallbacks. Use `re.compile` for regex.
- PR titles drive the changelog: `feat(terraform): add CKV_GCP_128 to ensure …`. Allowed scopes are listed in `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`. Do not assign reviewers; use `[WIP]`/`hold` when unfinished.
- Do not fill retired ID gaps. Allocate **max existing number + 1** for that prefix. `test_no_missing_ids` enforces sequences (GCP Python skips `CKV_GCP_5`, `_19`, `_67`).
- Stay inside approved context: this repo, its issues/PRs, `.cursor/`, and listed consumers in `.cursor/checkov-consumers.yml` (see `prepare-ci-ready-pr` / `maintain-ci-runners` `context-boundaries.md`).
